2026-08-28 novel-peptide validation
Input integrity: all supplied SHA-1/SHA-256 checksums matched task metadata.
Inputs: 196 unique candidate peptides; 4 MGF files containing 169591 spectra; 147506 human/isoform FASTA records plus 116 cRAP records.
Validator: PepQuery 2.0.2, novel-peptide mode, run independently per MGF and unioned by peptide.
Search settings: precursor 10 ppm; fragment 0.6 Da; trypsin; <=2 missed cleavages; charge 2-6; CID/HCD; fixed Carbamidomethyl(C), TMT11(K), TMT11(peptide N-term); variable Oxidation(M).
Competitive reference: supplied human UniProt+isoforms FASTA combined with supplied cRAP FASTA (147622 records).
Final PepQuery results after reference, random-peptide, and unrestricted-PTM competition:
  F10: 152 matched spectra; 53 accepted PSMs; 51 accepted peptides.
  F11: 128 matched spectra; 41 accepted PSMs; 33 accepted peptides.
  F13: 117 matched spectra; 41 accepted PSMs; 39 accepted peptides.
  F15: 106 matched spectra; 38 accepted PSMs; 34 accepted peptides.
Union: 139 unique verified peptides.
Report mapping: split all SGPS comma-delimited and MaxQuant semicolon-delimited protein assignments; normalized UniProt pipe identifiers to accessions; deduplicated exact peptide-protein pairs.
Deliverable: 144 unique peptide-protein pairs covering all 139 verified peptides.
